Patchset 3's LLM-Review found a genuine blocking correctness bug: candidate_verdict_flip discarded stored_blocking_criteria whenever candidate_findings was empty (a normal outcome, not an error) -- under-counting relieved criteria for any row where the candidate legitimately produced nothing. Fixed: compute stored_blocking unconditionally, only short-circuit the verify/decide call. Also fixed a test that had been (accidentally) encoding the bug as correct behavior, and added coverage for the 2 non-blocking advisory findings from the same review pass (_exclude_det_findings mixed-criteria single-finding case; cleanup_reconstructed_ticket's worktree-remove-failure fallback. 36/36 unit tests passing, lint/format/typecheck clean. Pushed as patchset 4 on change 2450.
EOF
